IMPORT prelude
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g1-interpretation`

-- g1-art1-defined-terms.l4: the title, the long title and Article 1 (Interpretation) of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014.
-- Source: the consolidated text "from 2 October 2026", INPUTS/charities-jersey-law-2014-2026-10-02.txt; every quotation below is a slice of that file (src:N is line N).
-- What this module does with the 35 definitions of Article 1 ("prescribed" and "specified" are one definition), by the disposition of each:
--   * encoded (4): "Minister" and "Comptroller", each by the text of the Law in force; "publish", by the opinion of the person publishing (fork F1.5); and "registered charity", by the
--     general or the restricted section of the register, and not the historic section;
--   * inert (23): the definitions that only point at a provision of this Law, which encodes them ("annual return", "charitable purpose", "constitution", "constitutional Law", "entity",
--     "general section", "governor", "Jersey entity", "misconduct", "purpose", "register", "registered charitable purposes", "registered public benefit statement", "reportable matter",
--     "required steps notice", "restricted section"), the definitions that point at the content of an Order ("donation", "solicit"), the rule of construction "prescribed" and "specified",
--     "regulated financial services business" (whose four limbs are out of scope), and the three roles "Commissioner", "court" and "tribunal", each carried by the actor constructor of the shared nouns;
--   * out of scope (8, and the four limbs of "regulated financial services business"): the definitions that name another enactment ("company", "court-approved fidéicommis", "foundation",
--     "incorporated 1862 association", "JFSC", "Loi of 1862", "property", "trust"). What they decide is an INPUT, the fact about the body that Article 2 reads; the other enactments are not among
--     the sources. "JFSC" is carried as the role `the Jersey Financial Services Commission`.
-- A definition that only points is a labelled stub: the quotation, its @ref, and a named value saying where the term is encoded or what input it is.
-- The lead-in is "unless the context otherwise requires". The one place found where the context displaces a definition is Article 5(2)(a), which says "a Minister"
-- with the indefinite article; that provision belongs to another group (its fork is F2.3) and is noted there, not here.
-- A defined term is not made into a rule where it only points: the pointer is the quotation, its @ref, and a stub saying where the term is encoded or what input it is.

§ `Charities (Jersey) Law 2014`

-- src:1 | Charities (Jersey) Law 2014
@ref Title (src:1)
`Title of the Law` MEANS "Charities (Jersey) Law 2014"

-- src:2 | A LAW to establish a commissioner and register of charities, to impose duties on governors of charities, to regulate use of the term “charity” and for related purposes
@ref Long title (src:2)
`Long title of the Law` MEANS
    "A LAW to establish a commissioner and register of charities, to impose duties on governors of charities, to regulate use of the term “charity” and for related purposes"

§ `Part 1 — Interpretation`

§§ `1 Interpretation`

-- src:6 | 1 Interpretation[1]
-- src:7 | In this Law, unless the context otherwise requires –
-- Endnote [1]: Article 1 was amended by R&O.40/2019, L.13/2019, R&O.29/2021, R&O.28/2023, R&O.10/2024 and R&O.102/2026 (the Table of Endnote References).
-- The amendments touch two definitions: "Minister" (five instruments) and "Comptroller" (one); both are computed below as a function of the text of the Law.
@ref Article 1, lead-in (src:6-7)
`Art 1 lead-in` MEANS "In this Law, unless the context otherwise requires –"

-- src:8 | “annual return” means a return sent under Article 13(7);
@ref Article 1, definition of “annual return” (src:8)
`Art 1 annual return` MEANS
    "a pointer: a return sent under Article 13(7); the duty to send it, and what it holds, are encoded with Article 13(7)"

-- src:9 | “charitable purpose” has the meaning given by Article 6;
@ref Article 1, definition of “charitable purpose” (src:9)
`Art 1 charitable purpose` MEANS
    "a pointer: the meaning given by Article 6, encoded there; the sixteen heads of Article 6(1) are the shared noun `Head of charitable purpose`"

-- src:10 | “Commissioner” means the person for the time being appointed to hold the office of the Jersey Charity Commissioner established by Article 3;
-- A role, not a rule: every power and duty of the Commissioner is typed by this actor. Who holds the office on a day is Schedule 1 (paragraphs 1 and 4(5)).
@ref Article 1, definition of “Commissioner” (src:10)
`Art 1 Commissioner` MEANS `the Commissioner`

-- src:11 | “company” means a company registered under the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991, or an existing company within the meaning of that Law, and in relation to a company the expressions “director”, “memorandum” and “articles of association” have the same meanings as in that Law;
-- Out of scope: the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991 is not among the sources. Whether a body is a company is the INPUT `a company` of the facts about a body (Article 2(1)(f)),
-- and who a director is, is the INPUT `a director of the company` of the facts about a person's role (Article 2(7)(c)).
@ref Article 1, definition of “company” (src:11)
`Art 1 company` MEANS
    "out of scope, so an input: a company under the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991 is the fact `a company` of Article 2(1)(f); a director is the fact `a director of the company` of Article 2(7)(c)"

-- src:12 | “Comptroller” has the meaning given by the Revenue Administration (Jersey) Law 2019;
-- The word the definition points at changed: until the end of 31 December 2019 it was the Income Tax (Jersey) Law 1961. See `Art 1 the Law that defines the Comptroller under the text of` below.
@ref Article 1, definition of “Comptroller” (src:12)
`Art 1 Comptroller` MEANS `the Comptroller`

-- src:13 | “constitution” has the meaning given by Article 2(4);
@ref Article 1, definition of “constitution” (src:13)
`Art 1 constitution` MEANS "a pointer: the meaning given by Article 2(4), encoded there"

-- src:14 | “constitutional Law” has the meaning given by Article 2(5);
@ref Article 1, definition of “constitutional Law” (src:14)
`Art 1 constitutional Law` MEANS "a pointer: the meaning given by Article 2(5), encoded there; it names no Law for some kinds of entity, so the answer there may be none"

-- src:15 | “court”, in the expression “the court”, means the Royal Court;
-- A role, not a rule: the court that makes the orders of Articles 14, 17 and 20 is this actor.
@ref Article 1, definition of “court” (src:15)
`Art 1 court` MEANS `the court`

-- src:16 | “court-approved fidéicommis” means a fidéicommis created under Article 3 of the Loi of 1862, or to which the court has extended the benefits of that Loi under Article 17 of that Loi;
-- Out of scope: the Loi (1862) is not among the sources. Whether a body is the fidéicommissaires of a court-approved fidéicommis is the INPUT of Article 2(1)(b).
@ref Article 1, definition of “court-approved fidéicommis” (src:16)
`Art 1 court-approved fidéicommis` MEANS
    "out of scope, so an input: a fidéicommis created under, or extended the benefits of, the Loi of 1862 is the fact of Article 2(1)(b)"

-- src:17 | “donation” is to be construed in accordance with the Order made under Article 9(3)(b)(ii);
@ref Article 1, definition of “donation” (src:17)
`Art 1 donation` MEANS
    "a pointer to the content of the Order under Article 9(3)(b)(ii), which is not among the sources and is an input to the rules that read it"

-- src:18 | “entity” has the meaning given by Article 2(1);
@ref Article 1, definition of “entity” (src:18)
`Art 1 entity` MEANS "a pointer: the meaning given by Article 2(1), encoded there; the kinds are the shared noun `Kind of entity`"

-- src:19 | “foundation” means a foundation incorporated under the Foundations (Jersey) Law 2009, and “charter”, “regulations” and “council member” have, in relation to a foundation, the same meanings as in that Law;
-- Out of scope: the Foundations (Jersey) Law 2009 is not among the sources. Whether a body is a foundation is the INPUT `a foundation` of Article 2(1)(d),
-- and who is a council member is the INPUT `a member of the council of the foundation` of Article 2(7)(b).
@ref Article 1, definition of “foundation” (src:19)
`Art 1 foundation` MEANS
    "out of scope, so an input: a foundation under the Foundations (Jersey) Law 2009 is the fact `a foundation` of Article 2(1)(d); a council member is the fact of Article 2(7)(b)"

-- src:20 | “general section” means the section of the register that is to be distinguished from the restricted and historic sections under Article 8(2);
@ref Article 1, definition of “general section” (src:20)
`Art 1 general section` MEANS
    "a pointer: the section distinguished under Article 8(2)(a); it is the standing `entered in the general section` of the shared noun `Standing on the register`"

-- src:21 | “governor” in relation to an entity (including a registered charity) has the meaning given by Article 2(7);
@ref Article 1, definition of “governor” (src:21)
`Art 1 governor` MEANS "a pointer: the meaning given by Article 2(7) to (9), encoded there; a governor is carried by the shared noun `Governor`"

-- src:22 | “incorporated 1862 association” means an association incorporated under Article 4 of the Loi of 1862;
-- Out of scope: the Loi (1862) is not among the sources. Whether a body is one is the INPUT `an incorporated 1862 association` of Article 2(1)(c).
@ref Article 1, definition of “incorporated 1862 association” (src:22)
`Art 1 incorporated 1862 association` MEANS
    "out of scope, so an input: an association incorporated under Article 4 of the Loi of 1862 is the fact `an incorporated 1862 association` of Article 2(1)(c)"

-- src:23 | “JFSC” means the Jersey Financial Services Commission established by the Financial Services Commission (Jersey) Law 1998;
-- A role, not a rule. The Financial Services Commission (Jersey) Law 1998 is out of scope.
@ref Article 1, definition of “JFSC” (src:23)
`Art 1 JFSC` MEANS `the Jersey Financial Services Commission`

-- src:24 | “Jersey entity” has the meaning given by Article 2(3);
@ref Article 1, definition of “Jersey entity” (src:24)
`Art 1 Jersey entity` MEANS "a pointer: the meaning given by Article 2(3), encoded there; it is the field `is a Jersey entity` of the shared noun `Entity`"

-- src:25 | “Loi of 1862” means the Loi (1862) sur les teneures en fidéicommis et l’incorporation d’associations;
-- Out of scope: the title of another enactment, not among the sources; named wherever Article 2 says "Loi of 1862".
@ref Article 1, definition of “Loi of 1862” (src:25)
`Art 1 Loi of 1862` MEANS "the Loi (1862) sur les teneures en fidéicommis et l’incorporation d’associations: out of scope, named only"

-- The refusal for a day before the first consolidated text, shared by every rule of this group that is a function of the text of the Law. The Table of Legislation History gives the
-- commencement of the Law (the remainder on 1 January 2019, R&O.17/2018) and the dates of the amending instruments; the nine consolidated texts begin on 1 January 2019, and the text the Law
-- had on an earlier day is not among the sources.
-- src:880 | Remainder in force 1 January 2019 (R&O.17/2018).
@ref Table of Legislation History (src:880)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Art 1 no text of the Law before 1 January 2019 is among the sources` MEANS
    REFUSE "no text of the Law before 1 January 2019 is among the sources"

-- src:26 | “Minister” means the Chief Minister;
-- The text of 2 October 2026. The definition has had five texts (the Table of Legislation History and the amending instruments):
--   until 30 May 2019                   "Chief Minister"                                              (words replaced by R&O.40/2019 Sch 2 para 1(e): so these are the words before, derived, not quoted from a consolidated text)
--   31 May 2019 to 1 March 2021         "Minister for External Relations"                            (R&O.40/2019 Sch 2 para 1(e), made and in force 31 May 2019)
--   2 March 2021 to 11 April 2023       "Minister for External Relations and Financial Services"     (R&O.29/2021 Sch 2 para 1(e), made and in force 2 March 2021)
--   12 April 2023 to 9.30 a.m. on 27 February 2024  "Chief Minister"                              (R&O.28/2023 Sch 2 para 1(4), made 5 April, in force 7 days after)
--   27 February 2024 (9.30 a.m.) to 1 October 2026  "Minister for External Relations"                 (R&O.10/2024 Sch 4 para (1), in force at 9.30 a.m. on 27 February 2024)
--   from 2 October 2026                 "Chief Minister"                                              (R&O.102/2026 Art 1, made 25 September, the rest in force 7 days after; and the line quoted above)
-- Each step replaces exactly the words the step before it put in, so the chain closes: the words R&O.40/2019 replaced are the words R&O.102/2026 put back.
-- The text of 16 October 2025 is the text of 27 February 2024 for this definition: R&O.56/2025 inserts Article 2(1)(ba) and touches no definition; it was made "by THE MINISTER
-- FOR EXTERNAL RELATIONS" under Article 2(2), which agrees. The day 27 February 2024 itself needs the hour: the text changes at 9.30 a.m. and the vintage of the text is the caller's.
-- No text before 1 January 2019 is among the sources, so the first vintage answers by refusal.
-- src:883 | Functions) (Chief Minister to External Relations) Order 2019
-- src:884 | R&O.40/2019
-- src:885 | 31 May 2019
-- src:897 | R&O.29/2021
-- src:898 | 2 March 2021
-- src:901 | R&O.28/2023
-- src:902 | 12 April 2023
-- src:905 | R&O.10/2024
-- src:906 | 9.30 a.m. on 27 February 2024
-- src:911 | R&O.102/2026
-- src:912 | 2 October 2026
-- src:931 | [1] Article 1 amended
-- src:932 | by R&O.40/2019, L.13/2019,
-- src:933 | R&O.29/2021, R&O.28/2023,
-- src:934 | R&O.10/2024, R&O.102/2026
@ref Article 1, definition of “Minister” (src:26, src:883-885, src:897-898, src:901-902, src:905-906, src:911-912, src:931-934)
@export The office that the definition of "Minister" in Article 1 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 names in a given text of the Law (the Chief Minister, the Minister for External Relations, or the Minister for External Relations and Financial Services); it refuses for a day before the first consolidated text of 1 January 2019
GIVEN `the vintage of the text` IS A `Vintage of the text` @desc Which text of the Law is in force, as decided by the vintage resolver for the day (or the instant, for 27 February 2024) in question
GIVETH AN `Office of the Minister`
`Art 1 the Minister under the text of` `the vintage of the text` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the vintage of the text`
    WHEN `before the first consolidated version` THEN `Art 1 no text of the Law before 1 January 2019 is among the sources`
    WHEN `the text of 1 January 2019` THEN `the Chief Minister`
    WHEN `the text of 31 May 2019` THEN `the Minister for External Relations`
    WHEN `the text of 16 December 2019` THEN `the Minister for External Relations`
    WHEN `the text of 1 January 2020` THEN `the Minister for External Relations`
    WHEN `the text of 2 March 2021` THEN `the Minister for External Relations and Financial Services`
    WHEN `the text of 12 April 2023` THEN `the Chief Minister`
    WHEN `the text of 27 February 2024` THEN `the Minister for External Relations`
    WHEN `the text of 16 October 2025` THEN `the Minister for External Relations`
    WHEN `the text of 2 October 2026` THEN `the Chief Minister`

-- src:12 | “Comptroller” has the meaning given by the Revenue Administration (Jersey) Law 2019;
-- Until the end of 31 December 2019 the definition read "has the meaning given by the Income Tax (Jersey) Law 1961": L.13/2019 Sch 3 para 1 substitutes the words
-- "Revenue Administration (Jersey) Law 2019" for the words "Income Tax (Jersey) Law 1961", and the Revenue Administration (Jersey) Law 2019 came into force on
-- 1 January 2020 (the Table of Legislation History; R&O.136/2019 Art 1, which brings the whole Law into force that day except Articles 17 to 19, none of which is Schedule 3).
-- The Law substituted is the only part of the sentence the instrument shows; the rest of the earlier sentence is read from the consolidated text.
-- src:891 | L.13/2019
-- src:892 | 1 January 2020 (R&O.136/2019)
DECLARE `Law defining the Comptroller` IS ONE OF
    `the Income Tax (Jersey) Law 1961`
    `the Revenue Administration (Jersey) Law 2019`

@ref Article 1, definition of “Comptroller” (src:12, src:891-892)
@export The Law that the definition of "Comptroller" in Article 1 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 points at in a given text of the Law (the Income Tax (Jersey) Law 1961 until 31 December 2019, the Revenue Administration (Jersey) Law 2019 from 1 January 2020); it refuses for a day before the first consolidated text
GIVEN `the vintage of the text` IS A `Vintage of the text` @desc Which text of the Law is in force, as decided by the vintage resolver for the day in question
GIVETH A `Law defining the Comptroller`
`Art 1 the Law that defines the Comptroller under the text of` `the vintage of the text` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the vintage of the text`
    WHEN `before the first consolidated version` THEN `Art 1 no text of the Law before 1 January 2019 is among the sources`
    WHEN `the text of 1 January 2019` THEN `the Income Tax (Jersey) Law 1961`
    WHEN `the text of 31 May 2019` THEN `the Income Tax (Jersey) Law 1961`
    WHEN `the text of 16 December 2019` THEN `the Income Tax (Jersey) Law 1961`
    WHEN `the text of 1 January 2020` THEN `the Revenue Administration (Jersey) Law 2019`
    WHEN `the text of 2 March 2021` THEN `the Revenue Administration (Jersey) Law 2019`
    WHEN `the text of 12 April 2023` THEN `the Revenue Administration (Jersey) Law 2019`
    WHEN `the text of 27 February 2024` THEN `the Revenue Administration (Jersey) Law 2019`
    WHEN `the text of 16 October 2025` THEN `the Revenue Administration (Jersey) Law 2019`
    WHEN `the text of 2 October 2026` THEN `the Revenue Administration (Jersey) Law 2019`

-- src:27 | “misconduct” has the meaning given by Article 2(10), and a reference to a governor engaging in misconduct is to be read in accordance with Article 18(4);
@ref Article 1, definition of “misconduct” (src:27)
`Art 1 misconduct` MEANS
    "a pointer: the meaning given by Article 2(10), encoded there; a reference to a governor engaging in misconduct is read under Article 18(4), encoded there"

-- src:28 | “prescribed” and “specified” mean prescribed or specified in an Order or Regulations, as the case may be;
-- A rule of construction, carried by the convention of the whole encoding: the content of an Order or of Regulations is an input, and the power to make one is a MAY rule.
@ref Article 1, definition of “prescribed” and “specified” (src:28)
`Art 1 prescribed and specified` MEANS
    "a rule of construction: what an Order or Regulations prescribe or specify is an input to the rule that reads it; the power to make them is encoded where the Law confers it"

-- src:29 | “property” has the meaning given by the Trusts (Jersey) Law 1984;
-- Out of scope: the Trusts (Jersey) Law 1984 is not among the sources; "property" is an input noun wherever the Law uses it.
@ref Article 1, definition of “property” (src:29)
`Art 1 property` MEANS "out of scope, so an input noun: the meaning given by the Trusts (Jersey) Law 1984"

-- src:30 | “publish”, in respect of any information, means publish in a manner that, in the opinion of the person publishing, is likely to bring the information or how the information may be obtained to the attention of the public or of those affected by the information;
-- The test is the opinion of the person publishing: F1.5 (reading A, taken). Reading B asks whether the manner is in fact likely to reach the audience.
-- "Publish" or "published" appears in Articles 4(1)(d), 5(4), 5(6)(b), 5(7), 7(4), 9(4)(a), 10(2)(b), 11(2), 11(6)(a), 11(9) and Schedule 1 paragraphs 4(8) and 4(11), and Article 2(8)(b)(i) of this group uses it.
DECLARE `Facts about a publication` HAS
    `made available by the person in some manner` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the person made the information, or how it may be obtained, available to anyone in any manner at all
    `the person publishing is of the opinion that the manner is likely to bring it to the attention of the public or of those affected` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc The opinion of the person publishing: that the manner is likely to bring the information, or how it may be obtained, to the attention of the public or of those affected by the information
    `the manner is in fact likely to bring it to the attention of the public or of those affected` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the manner is, judged objectively, likely to bring the information, or how it may be obtained, to the attention of the public or of those affected; read only under reading B of F1.5

@ref Article 1, definition of “publish” (src:30)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about a publication`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 1 published on the opinion of the person publishing` facts MEANS
        facts's `made available by the person in some manner`
    AND facts's `the person publishing is of the opinion that the manner is likely to bring it to the attention of the public or of those affected`

@ref Article 1, definition of “publish” (src:30)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about a publication`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 1 published on the likelihood of the manner` facts MEANS
        facts's `made available by the person in some manner`
    AND facts's `the manner is in fact likely to bring it to the attention of the public or of those affected`

@ref Article 1, definition of “publish” (src:30)
@export Whether information has been published in the sense of Article 1 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014: made available in a manner that, in the opinion of the person publishing, is likely to bring the information or how it may be obtained to the attention of the public or of those affected (the reading can be set to the objective likelihood of the manner instead)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` @desc The reading taken at each fork; the field `meaning of published` decides whether the publisher's opinion or the manner's likelihood counts
      facts IS A `Facts about a publication` @desc What the person did, what the person thought of the manner, and whether the manner is in fact likely to reach the audience
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 1 the information has been published` interp facts MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `meaning of published`
    WHEN `the opinion of the person publishing` THEN `Art 1 published on the opinion of the person publishing` facts
    WHEN `the likelihood of the manner, judged objectively` THEN `Art 1 published on the likelihood of the manner` facts

-- src:31 | “purpose”, in relation to an entity, has the meaning given by Article 2(6);
@ref Article 1, definition of “purpose” (src:31)
`Art 1 purpose` MEANS "a pointer: the meaning given by Article 2(6), encoded there; one purpose is the shared noun `Purpose`"

-- src:32 | “register” means the register kept by the Commissioner under Article 8, or (as a verb) to enter an entity on that register, and “registration” and “deregistration” are to be construed accordingly;
@ref Article 1, definition of “register” (src:32)
`Art 1 register` MEANS
    "a pointer: the register kept under Article 8, and as a verb to enter an entity on it; where an entity stands on it is the shared noun `Standing on the register`"

-- src:33 | “registered charitable purposes” has the meaning assigned by Article 8(3)(e);
@ref Article 1, definition of “registered charitable purposes” (src:33)
`Art 1 registered charitable purposes` MEANS
    "a pointer: the statement of purposes entered under Article 8(3)(e); it is the field `registered charitable purposes` of the shared noun `Registered charity`"

-- src:34 | “registered charity” means an entity entered for the time being in the general section or the restricted section of the register;
-- "An entity entered": a body that is not an entity under Article 2(1) is not a registered charity, however it stands on the register, so an empty list of kinds answers FALSE.
-- The historic section holds formerly registered charities, and "registered charity" does not take it in (trap T7 of the survey): such an entity is not a registered charity.
-- "For the time being" is a time-indexed standing: the caller gives the standing on the day in question. Which day Article 2(10) asks about is fork F1.7.
@ref Article 1, definition of “registered charity” (src:34)
GIVEN standing IS A `Standing on the register`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 1 the standing is that of a registered charity` standing MEANS
    CONSIDER standing
    WHEN `not on the register` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an applicant for registration` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `entered in the general section` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `entered in the restricted section` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `formerly registered and entered in the historic section` THEN FALSE

@ref Article 1, definition of “registered charity” (src:34)
@export Whether an entity is a registered charity in the sense of Article 1 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014: an entity entered for the time being in the general section or the restricted section of the register (not one that is only an applicant, or formerly registered and in the historic section)
GIVEN `the entity` IS AN Entity @desc The entity as Article 2 leaves it: its standing on the register on the day in question and the kinds of entity it falls within
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 1 the entity is a registered charity` `the entity` MEANS
        NOT null (`the entity`'s `kinds of entity`)
    AND `Art 1 the standing is that of a registered charity` (`the entity`'s `standing on the register`)

-- src:35 | “registered public benefit statement” has the meaning assigned by Article 8(3)(f);
@ref Article 1, definition of “registered public benefit statement” (src:35)
`Art 1 registered public benefit statement` MEANS
    "a pointer: the statement of public benefit entered under Article 8(3)(f); it is the field `registered public benefit statement` of the shared noun `Registered charity`"

-- src:36 | “regulated financial services business” means business for which a person –
-- src:37 | (a) is registered under the Banking Business (Jersey) Law 1991;
-- src:38 | (b) holds a permit or certificate under the Collective Investment Funds (Jersey) Law 1988;
-- src:39 | (c) is registered under the Financial Services (Jersey) Law 1998; or
-- src:40 | (d) is authorized by a permit under the Insurance Business (Jersey) Law 1996;
-- The four limbs are registrations under other enactments, which are out of scope. The term is read only by Articles 11(7)(a) and 14(3)(e), where it is part of the content
-- of Regulations and of an order, and so an input there: whether a business is one is a fact about the business that those Articles take as given.
@ref Article 1, definition of “regulated financial services business” (src:36-40)
`Art 1 regulated financial services business` MEANS
    "inert: business for which a person is registered under the Banking Business (Jersey) Law 1991, holds a permit or certificate under the Collective Investment Funds (Jersey) Law 1988, is registered under the Financial Services (Jersey) Law 1998 or is authorized by a permit under the Insurance Business (Jersey) Law 1996; each limb is out of scope and the term is an input where Articles 11(7)(a) and 14(3)(e) read it"

-- src:41 | “reportable matter” has the meaning given by Article 19;
@ref Article 1, definition of “reportable matter” (src:41)
`Art 1 reportable matter` MEANS
    "a pointer: the meaning given by Article 19(1), encoded there; the eight descriptions are the shared noun `Kind of reportable matter`"

-- src:42 | “required steps notice” means a notice served under Article 27;
@ref Article 1, definition of “required steps notice” (src:42)
`Art 1 required steps notice` MEANS
    "a pointer: a notice served under Article 27, encoded there; a notice is the shared noun `Required steps notice`"

-- src:43 | “restricted section” means the section of the register that is to be distinguished from the general and historic sections under Article 8(2);
@ref Article 1, definition of “restricted section” (src:43)
`Art 1 restricted section` MEANS
    "a pointer: the section distinguished under Article 8(2)(b); it is the standing `entered in the restricted section` of the shared noun `Standing on the register`"

-- src:44 | “solicit” is to be construed in accordance with the Order made under Article 9(3)(b)(i);
@ref Article 1, definition of “solicit” (src:44)
`Art 1 solicit` MEANS
    "a pointer to the content of the Order under Article 9(3)(b)(i), which is not among the sources and is an input to the rules that read it"

-- src:45 | “tribunal” means the Charity Tribunal established by Article 32;
-- A role, not a rule: the body that hears appeals under Part 8 is this actor. (Schedule 2 is headed "Charity Commission tribunal", and Article 32 "Charity Tribunal".)
@ref Article 1, definition of “tribunal” (src:45)
`Art 1 tribunal` MEANS `the Charity Tribunal`

-- src:46 | “trust” means a trust over which the court has jurisdiction under Article 5 of the Trusts (Jersey) Law 1984.
-- Out of scope: the Trusts (Jersey) Law 1984 is not among the sources. Whether a body is the trustees of such a trust is the INPUT of Article 2(1)(a);
-- who a trustee is, is the INPUT `a trustee of the trust or a fidéicommissaire of the fidéicommis` of Article 2(7)(a).
@ref Article 1, definition of “trust” (src:46)
`Art 1 trust` MEANS
    "out of scope, so an input: a trust over which the court has jurisdiction under Article 5 of the Trusts (Jersey) Law 1984 is the fact of Article 2(1)(a); a trustee is the fact of Article 2(7)(a)"
